1
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,685
Didn't you say you were going to dinner?

2
00:00:59,769 --> 00:01:03,147
I need to check something with you.

3
00:01:03,898 --> 00:01:06,066
-What?
-You started it.

4
00:01:31,634 --> 00:01:34,011
Are you crazy? I'll punch you.

5
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,513
Go ahead.

6
00:01:36,263 --> 00:01:38,098
I don't think you will anyway.

7
00:01:39,725 --> 00:01:42,520
That was my first time kissing a guy,

8
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:45,022
because someone got drunk
and came at me that night.

9
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:47,149
-I was…
-So for the past few days,

10
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:50,194
I know it's a little pathetic,
but I've been flustered.

11
00:01:53,155 --> 00:01:54,532
But I've just confirmed

12
00:01:55,491 --> 00:01:56,742
and reached a conclusion.

13
00:02:03,582 --> 00:02:05,376
I just wasted time

14
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,171
over something so trivial.

15
00:02:20,099 --> 00:02:21,725
How is this something trivial?

16
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:25,646
Is he out of his mind?

17
00:02:28,732 --> 00:02:31,944
Sometimes in life,

18
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:35,197
crazy love comes
charging at us like a raging bull.

19
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:40,077
When inexperienced lovers sense
that kind of true love,

20
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,787
their first instinct is to reject it.

21
00:02:41,871 --> 00:02:44,081
Why? It's a survival instinct.

22
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,374
EXPERT ON ROMANCE

23
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:47,918
In life, it's all or nothing.

24
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:51,422
You either wreck your own life
or ruin the other person's.

25
00:02:51,797 --> 00:02:53,716
But that's when you start

26
00:02:54,592 --> 00:02:57,136
seeing yourself struggle

27
00:02:57,219 --> 00:03:00,264
with all sorts of contradictions,

28
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,224
saying one thing and doing another.

29
00:03:02,725 --> 00:03:04,768
Why did he follow me after that?

30
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:08,522
Aren't you going home?

31
00:03:08,731 --> 00:03:10,065
As someone who is generous,

32
00:03:10,149 --> 00:03:12,526
I am giving you a chance
to apologize for your mistake.

33
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:16,196
-Buy me a meal.
-Why would I do that?

34
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,115
When I saved you from face-planting,

35
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:20,200
you knocked me flat instead.

36
00:03:20,284 --> 00:03:21,702
Not only that,

37
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:25,247
you jumped on me and went for my lips.

38
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:26,957
Like I said,

39
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:29,668
it was my mistake.

40
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:31,712
So I'm giving you the chance to apologize.

41
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:33,714
I'll treat you tomorrow.

42
00:03:33,797 --> 00:03:36,091
Buy me a meal today. Right now.

43
00:03:39,136 --> 00:03:41,221
Who was the guy next to you?

44
00:03:41,305 --> 00:03:43,891
Is he a friend?
You should choose your friends wisely.

45
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:47,102
I'm only saying this because
I think of you as my little brother.

46
00:03:47,186 --> 00:03:50,648
You know what?
You should bring him sometime.

47
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:51,899
-I am good at--
-I will…

48
00:03:52,942 --> 00:03:54,735
I will buy you that meal.

49
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,864
EPISODE 6

50
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:12,628
Why aren't you eating?

51
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:14,463
Is there a problem?

52
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:17,216
We could've just bought food
at the convenience store.

53
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:20,552
I did consider that idea,

54
00:04:20,636 --> 00:04:22,596
but whenever I'm on stakeout…

55
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,894
What's your favorite food, then?

56
00:04:28,978 --> 00:04:30,771
No need for excessive interest.

57
00:04:31,438 --> 00:04:32,398
-Hey.
-Hey!

58
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:33,732
-Come over here.
-Come here.

59
00:04:34,608 --> 00:04:37,695
I can tell you
that it's certainly not this junk food,

60
00:04:37,778 --> 00:04:39,571
loaded with fat for your liver and belly.

61
00:04:39,655 --> 00:04:41,782
Mr. Yoon,
what's your 100-meter sprint time?

62
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,450
I'd rather not answer that question.

63
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:45,035
I do not want to run.

64
00:04:45,119 --> 00:04:47,287
That's a bummer. I'll run on my own then.

65
00:04:47,371 --> 00:04:48,288
What?

66
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,083
-Come out.
-Come here.

67
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:53,252
-Come here.
-Hey. Do you have a death wish?

68
00:04:53,335 --> 00:04:54,670
What the hell?

69
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:55,713
Sir!

70
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:03,429
They want to kill you.

71
00:05:04,013 --> 00:05:06,140
-Is that consensual?
-I don't think so.

72
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:08,809
There are plenty of cabs
at the intersection.

73
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:10,394
You can get a premium taxi, too.

74
00:05:10,477 --> 00:05:13,230
You can come out in five, no, ten minutes.

75
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,440
-Special Forces!
-Hey!

76
00:05:14,523 --> 00:05:16,066
-Where is he?
-Where did he go?

77
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:17,776
-Over there!
-Where's the jerk?

78
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:18,902
That slippery punk.

79
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:19,820
Damn it.

80
00:05:19,903 --> 00:05:21,405
-Hey! Over there!
-He's running!

81
00:05:21,488 --> 00:05:22,823
What's wrong with him?

82
00:05:24,992 --> 00:05:25,826
Get him!

83
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:27,244
YORIJORI CHINESE RESTAURANT

84
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,495
-You're dead meat!
-Hey!

85
00:05:28,579 --> 00:05:30,748
-Hey!
-Come here!

86
00:05:39,715 --> 00:05:42,968
I planned a full-course dinner
that cost hundreds of thousands of won.

87
00:05:43,052 --> 00:05:45,929
Pork bone haejangguk,
noodles, and fried rice.

88
00:05:47,306 --> 00:05:48,640
It's still a full-course meal.

89
00:05:48,724 --> 00:05:52,936
Are you really going to
forgive little old me with just this?

90
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,564
A meal is a meal.
Forgiveness has nothing to do with it.

91
00:05:55,647 --> 00:05:57,983
You'll feed me first
before interrogating me?

92
00:05:58,567 --> 00:06:02,029
Is this like how detectives buy suspects
gukbap at the station?

93
00:06:02,112 --> 00:06:05,240
If you'd like to confess first, go ahead.

94
00:06:05,324 --> 00:06:06,575
Goodness.

95
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:12,164
I could say my phone cut out
because my phone was malfunctioning,

96
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:16,835
but I'd be ashamed to lie as a lawyer.

97
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:20,923
So I'll just say I couldn't take the call
and hung up on my own.

98
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:24,802
There may be many reasons
why you couldn't take my call.

99
00:06:25,177 --> 00:06:26,345
That's right.

100
00:06:27,846 --> 00:06:31,600
Out of those reasons,
I was meeting someone.

101
00:06:34,228 --> 00:06:35,646
Executive Director Yoon Na-jung?

102
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:44,238
Secretaries really have
some scary connections.

103
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:46,657
Fine.

104
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:49,743
I'll be honest with you

105
00:06:50,828 --> 00:06:52,746
and tell you why we met.

106
00:06:53,122 --> 00:06:57,251
But before that,
I'd like you to be honest too.

107
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:05,759
Han Eun-young's desk.

108
00:07:07,845 --> 00:07:08,971
Why did you replace it?

109
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,810
-Hey!
-You bastard!

110
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:16,812
-Stop!
-He's so fast!

111
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:21,733
-Over there!
-Hey, this way!

112
00:07:21,817 --> 00:07:23,610
-Go get him!
-Get him!

113
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:26,989
-You jerk!
-Block him!

114
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:28,407
-Stop!
-You punk!

115
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:29,825
-Come here!
-Stop!

116
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:33,954
-Go!
-I said I'm sorry!

117
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,455
-Get out!
-Okay.

118
00:07:35,539 --> 00:07:38,792
Good grief. This is crazy.

119
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:43,297
That fool doesn't understand women at all.

120
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:46,383
-Then I'll leave.
-Just leave! Get lost!

121
00:07:47,009 --> 00:07:49,511
A man has pride.
If she asked him to go, he should go.

122
00:07:49,595 --> 00:07:51,763
What was he supposed to do?
Beg for forgiveness?

123
00:07:51,847 --> 00:07:54,516
She always came here alone,
looking all pathetic.

124
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,935
I thought it was good
that she brought a guy with her.

125
00:07:57,019 --> 00:07:59,104
But it looks like you guys won't last.

126
00:08:01,148 --> 00:08:02,733
Hye-jung comes here alone?

127
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,818
I'm the first guy she brought?

128
00:08:04,902 --> 00:08:07,154
If you want a shot with her,

129
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:09,781
make sure you watch
every episode of that drama.

130
00:08:10,157 --> 00:08:12,034
She watches it all the time.

131
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,911
Is that so?

132
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,163
I see.

133
00:08:17,289 --> 00:08:20,083
It looks like
you don't know anything about her.

134
00:08:21,251 --> 00:08:23,462
Take the potato and cabbage out.

135
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:26,089
So just give her meat?

136
00:08:26,173 --> 00:08:28,050
-Take the beer away.
-Why?

137
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,260
-Get the red-cap soju.
-What?

138
00:08:30,344 --> 00:08:32,846
Put it back before she comes back.

139
00:08:43,232 --> 00:08:45,817
I heard you like soap operas
and hate vegetables.

140
00:08:47,444 --> 00:08:51,406
How does your regular spot's owner
know more about you than I do? I'm hurt.

141
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:54,201
You sure are curious.

142
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:56,954
Because you never give me a proper answer.

143
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:00,832
So answer me this time.

144
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:04,503
Why did you replace Secretary Han's desk?

145
00:09:05,504 --> 00:09:06,880
Attorney Kim.

146
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:10,842
Why did you look up who replaced the desk?

147
00:09:12,678 --> 00:09:13,887
I asked you first.

148
00:09:13,971 --> 00:09:17,182
The thirstier person digs the well.

149
00:09:18,934 --> 00:09:20,143
Whoever is more curious

150
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:22,521
will answer first, right?

151
00:09:27,609 --> 00:09:28,902
-He's here.
-You idiot!

152
00:09:28,986 --> 00:09:29,945
-Hold on.
-Got you.

153
00:09:31,405 --> 00:09:33,365
-That's him.
-Hey, I missed you.

154
00:09:33,448 --> 00:09:34,533
Did you?

155
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:36,910
-Come here. You're coming with us.
-You're dead.

156
00:09:36,994 --> 00:09:38,161
Stop wasting time.

157
00:09:38,245 --> 00:09:39,705
Come here.

158
00:09:39,788 --> 00:09:43,625
Don't do it!

159
00:09:43,709 --> 00:09:44,876
I'm sorry, Captain.

160
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,963
Did you miss this too?

161
00:09:48,714 --> 00:09:50,340
I knew you'd do the same thing.

162
00:09:50,424 --> 00:09:51,508
How cute.

163
00:09:53,677 --> 00:09:54,970
-It's not working.
-It's not!

164
00:09:55,554 --> 00:09:57,556
-It's not working!
-Damn it.

165
00:09:58,307 --> 00:10:00,058
-Get your weapons ready.
-I got scared.

166
00:10:00,142 --> 00:10:01,184
-Yes, sir.
-That's low.

167
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,854
How many of you are there?
One, two, three, four, five, six.

168
00:10:03,937 --> 00:10:04,771
Wait!

169
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,201
My goodness. Mr. Yoon!

170
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:29,963
No, stop.

171
00:10:43,894 --> 00:10:44,978
Take it easy.

172
00:10:45,062 --> 00:10:47,022
What are you doing?
Why didn't you go home?

173
00:10:47,105 --> 00:10:50,817
You'll get hurt. Just stay out of sight
like those fish over there.

174
00:10:50,901 --> 00:10:51,902
Hey, Fish.

175
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:55,280
What?

176
00:10:55,364 --> 00:10:57,783
Why don't you play with that toy
somewhere else?

177
00:10:59,076 --> 00:11:00,202
You'll be in trouble.

178
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:04,414
-That hurts!
-Boss!

179
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:05,499
What on earth?

180
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:06,750
-Get him!
-What the heck?

181
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:09,002
What was that?
Why are you good at fighting?

182
00:11:09,086 --> 00:11:12,964
Are you trying to compliment me?
You make it sound like an insult.

183
00:11:13,048 --> 00:11:15,425
It was an insult, sir.

184
00:11:15,509 --> 00:11:17,594
Hey, get them!

185
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:28,855
Come here!

186
00:11:44,246 --> 00:11:45,622
My hand!

187
00:11:46,373 --> 00:11:47,499
Get him!

188
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,381
Jeez. Are you okay?

189
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:57,008
You usually don't even lift a finger.

190
00:11:57,092 --> 00:11:58,552
Didn't I already tell you?

191
00:11:58,635 --> 00:12:00,720
It's not that I can't.
I just choose not to.

192
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:13,942
-Hey, you scumbag!
-You bastard!

193
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:18,697
Mr. Yoon, are you okay?

194
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:19,823
-I'm fine.
-Let me see.

195
00:12:20,699 --> 00:12:21,700
You're bleeding.

196
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:24,035
They hit a civilian?

197
00:12:24,119 --> 00:12:26,163
-Come here, sir.
-I'm fine.

198
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:29,666
You just sit neatly on this chair

199
00:12:29,749 --> 00:12:31,376
and enjoy the show.

200
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:32,419
I'm really okay.

201
00:12:35,005 --> 00:12:36,548
As for the rest of them,

202
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:39,092
I'll neatly take care of them.

203
00:12:39,176 --> 00:12:40,343
I said I'm fine.

204
00:12:41,136 --> 00:12:42,095
Special Forces.

205
00:12:42,179 --> 00:12:44,598
You damn little clams.

206
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:47,392
Come over here!

207
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:49,811
What clams?

208
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:56,526
Hold on.

209
00:12:59,446 --> 00:13:01,907
-Come at me!
-You scumbag!

210
00:13:02,491 --> 00:13:04,326
I guess he was going easy on me until now.

211
00:13:07,496 --> 00:13:09,372
That guy.

212
00:13:09,456 --> 00:13:11,166
He's amazing.

213
00:13:12,918 --> 00:13:15,128
I'm terrified of him.

214
00:13:15,212 --> 00:13:17,756
-He's my personal secretary.
-Come here!

215
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:18,798
Stop.

216
00:13:18,882 --> 00:13:20,717
Stay away!

217
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:25,555
It's the number Han Eun-young last called.

218
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:28,725
Don't mind the call history.
Look through her messages.

219
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:29,726
Okay.

220
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:33,146
What are we, Hong Gil-dong?

221
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:36,149
We can't refer to our investigation
as an investigation,

222
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:39,402
or say we found the phone
when we've already found it.

223
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:41,780
At least he made a name for himself.

224
00:13:41,863 --> 00:13:45,200
Exactly. He made a name for himself.

225
00:13:45,659 --> 00:13:49,538
As for you, it'll be a miracle
if you don't get chewed out for this.

226
00:13:49,621 --> 00:13:50,956
Do you have a death wish?

227
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:52,666
My grandma used to say

228
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:55,627
your name shapes your life.

229
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,628
That's enough.

230
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:59,381
You, Park Bong-yi,
are destined to be paid in peanuts.

231
00:14:01,716 --> 00:14:04,219
Did you just catch what I threw at you?

232
00:14:04,302 --> 00:14:06,972
How dare you?
You need to be taught a lesson.

233
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,473
This feels nice.

234
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:10,433
-This is nice.
-Take that.

235
00:14:10,517 --> 00:14:11,768
-The other side.
-Hold on.

236
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:12,936
-Look at you.
-What?

237
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,604
JAE-HEE: CODE001

238
00:14:16,356 --> 00:14:17,983
-Code one.
-What?

239
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:19,150
Code one?

240
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:24,948
She's supposed to be an officer.
She got hauled into a police station?

241
00:14:25,031 --> 00:14:26,908
Forget it. Just let her go to jail.

242
00:14:26,992 --> 00:14:29,911
Come on, we can't do that.
We need to save her.

243
00:14:29,995 --> 00:14:32,330
It's over for us
if her identity gets revealed.

244
00:14:33,123 --> 00:14:33,999
Which station is it?

245
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:37,752
Chief Cho Chan-seok's station.
Near Kang's house.

246
00:14:37,836 --> 00:14:39,337
Yoon Yi-jun knows how you look.

247
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:41,089
I'll go.

248
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:46,720
But what if he sees me
cleaning the bathroom at work?

249
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:48,346
Damn it.

250
00:14:49,097 --> 00:14:50,849
You're all unbelievable.

251
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:53,268
HEUNGSEO POLICE STATION

252
00:14:53,351 --> 00:14:55,061
-He did it!
-It was him!

253
00:14:55,145 --> 00:14:57,689
-Those bastards started it!
-It was him!

254
00:14:58,732 --> 00:14:59,691
He did it!

255
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,736
Keep your voices down!

256
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:04,571
-Jeez.
-It was him.

257
00:15:04,654 --> 00:15:06,823
-I didn't do anything.
-It was his fault.

258
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:10,285
So to sum it up,
those voice-phishing gang members

259
00:15:10,368 --> 00:15:13,455
held a grudge against you

260
00:15:13,538 --> 00:15:15,165
for getting their middleman arrested,

261
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:18,918
went after you for revenge,
and ended up like that?

262
00:15:19,002 --> 00:15:20,295
Exactly.

263
00:15:20,962 --> 00:15:22,714
Thank you. We'll get going now.

264
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:23,965
Sir.

265
00:15:24,049 --> 00:15:27,552
Government procedures
aren't exactly that simple.

266
00:15:28,303 --> 00:15:31,348
I know too well.
That's what's driving me crazy.

267
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:41,024
Sir, why are you daydreaming
in a police station?

268
00:15:44,027 --> 00:15:45,070
Mr. Yoon, are you okay?

269
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:46,988
You're bleeding.

270
00:15:47,072 --> 00:15:48,531
-Is it here?
-Yes.

271
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:52,702
You just sit neatly on this chair

272
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:55,330
and enjoy the show.

273
00:15:55,413 --> 00:15:57,332
Come over here!

274
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:05,423
Why is he blushing in a police station?

275
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:07,342
He's cute.

276
00:16:10,345 --> 00:16:11,846
Did he have a drink?

277
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:15,141
Not at all. But as you can see,
he's not in his right mind.

278
00:16:15,225 --> 00:16:16,768
I need to take him to the hospital.

279
00:16:16,851 --> 00:16:19,229
I'm not going anywhere.
I won't be showing them mercy.

280
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:20,980
Call everyone on the legal team.

281
00:16:21,606 --> 00:16:23,483
If you do, the reporters will flock here

282
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,069
-and it will be all over the Internet.
-Be quiet.

283
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:27,445
I'll take care of this.

284
00:16:28,321 --> 00:16:30,699
Why are you insisting?

285
00:16:30,782 --> 00:16:33,618
Special Forces, why are you stopping me?

286
00:16:33,702 --> 00:16:35,370
Because I'm worried.

287
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:38,540
Because I'm worried.

288
00:16:38,623 --> 00:16:39,499
Worried?

289
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,584
Yes, I'm worried about myself.

290
00:16:42,252 --> 00:16:43,712
Just cooperate already.

291
00:16:44,421 --> 00:16:47,799
Sir, there is actually something
you should be worried about.

292
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:51,761
Even fighting back can constitute assault.

293
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:53,555
Therefore, according to the procedure,

294
00:16:53,638 --> 00:16:56,641
give me your name and ID number.

295
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:06,276
Officer, could I speak with you
for a moment?

296
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:07,944
Just a moment.

297
00:17:08,528 --> 00:17:10,363
What is it?

298
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:12,490
Where's the chief?

299
00:17:12,574 --> 00:17:14,117
I have to speak to them personally.

300
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,744
You're looking for our chief?

301
00:17:15,827 --> 00:17:17,078
Yes.

302
00:17:19,122 --> 00:17:21,791
"I know your chief! He's my neighbor!"

303
00:17:22,292 --> 00:17:23,793
That trick won't work.

304
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:26,045
He doesn't live in this neighborhood.

305
00:17:26,129 --> 00:17:27,756
Should I call the legal team?

306
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:34,179
Even with a lawyer,
you have to give us your information.

307
00:17:34,262 --> 00:17:35,722
Just give me a second.

308
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:40,435
Your name and ID number.
Then you can go home.

309
00:17:45,482 --> 00:17:48,026
I told you not to cause trouble!

310
00:17:52,906 --> 00:17:54,199
My name is

311
00:17:54,282 --> 00:17:56,451
-Kang Jae-hee.
-Jae-i?

312
00:17:56,534 --> 00:17:58,036
-Jae-hee.
-Jae-hee.

313
00:17:59,913 --> 00:18:00,997
And…

314
00:18:01,873 --> 00:18:03,041
my ID number is 970…

315
00:18:04,793 --> 00:18:06,920
-And 812…
-What?

316
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:11,758
It's 970…

317
00:18:12,467 --> 00:18:13,927
And 81…

318
00:18:18,014 --> 00:18:19,182
How may I help you?

319
00:18:32,153 --> 00:18:33,321
I'm sorry, Seok-jin.

320
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:35,114
Chief Cho is my father's friend.

321
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,450
Why did you two come here?

322
00:18:37,534 --> 00:18:38,493
The thing is,

323
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:42,622
I was trying to stop him
from asking about you.

324
00:18:44,332 --> 00:18:45,750
I didn't think this through.

325
00:18:51,047 --> 00:18:52,090
Clean this up first.

326
00:18:52,841 --> 00:18:54,133
Send him home and come back.

327
00:18:54,217 --> 00:18:55,260
Yes, sir.

328
00:19:03,518 --> 00:19:06,104
GO JAE-DEOK
KANG JAE-HEE

329
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,428
I know it's late,
but should I call Secretary Jung?

330
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:40,430
Where do you live?

331
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,058
It's near here.

332
00:19:44,976 --> 00:19:47,228
Okay. Let's walk then.

333
00:19:58,031 --> 00:19:59,240
You dropped this.

334
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:01,117
GO JAE-DEOK
KANG JAE-HEE

335
00:20:06,664 --> 00:20:09,250
What's the other name on your dog tag?

336
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:12,795
May I refuse to answer?

337
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,505
Then will you answer this?

338
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,383
Who was he earlier?

339
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:20,094
You were with him
in front of the office too.

340
00:20:28,645 --> 00:20:29,771
He's a close friend.

341
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:31,397
A close friend?

342
00:20:32,649 --> 00:20:35,777
When did you learn fencing?
You were pretty good at it.

343
00:20:36,819 --> 00:20:38,112
You keep changing the subject

344
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:40,615
whenever this topic comes up,
just like earlier,

345
00:20:42,367 --> 00:20:45,119
by asking things about me
you're not even curious about.

346
00:20:47,705 --> 00:20:49,165
This is my home.

347
00:21:06,724 --> 00:21:07,684
Fine.

348
00:21:08,893 --> 00:21:10,520
I am the thirstier one.

349
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:14,524
I looked up
who replaced the desk because--

350
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:18,319
I approached you intentionally,
Attorney Kim.

351
00:21:19,821 --> 00:21:23,157
From the moment you told Secretary Kang
that I was no fun.

352
00:21:23,241 --> 00:21:25,994
Even at the club,
I went there with a purpose.

353
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:28,496
What purpose?

354
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:32,500
The fact that you have to ask already
gives me my answer.

355
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:36,087
But everything wasn't fake.

356
00:21:37,005 --> 00:21:40,633
Whenever you were sweet to me,
I wanted to be sincere too.

357
00:21:42,093 --> 00:21:44,137
So this is where I have to stop.

358
00:21:47,557 --> 00:21:48,474
Stop?

359
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:56,357
Yes, this is our end.

360
00:22:41,778 --> 00:22:43,196
This is Lee Hye-jung.

361
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,781
This is Seoul Metropolitan Police.

362
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:46,908
Ms. Lee Hye-jung,
you spoke with Han Eun-young,

363
00:22:46,991 --> 00:22:50,036
the victim in the Taekang Group murder,
around February 5th, correct?

364
00:22:57,794 --> 00:23:00,254
Who else did you tell

365
00:23:00,338 --> 00:23:03,674
that Mr. Yoon
was looking into the slush fund?

366
00:23:07,470 --> 00:23:08,387
Han Eun-young.

367
00:23:09,222 --> 00:23:12,892
Did you tell someone else
about what you know?

368
00:23:13,768 --> 00:23:16,687
I told one other person besides you.

369
00:23:18,648 --> 00:23:19,524
Who?

370
00:23:20,942 --> 00:23:22,276
Mr. Yoon's…

371
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:26,322
Can you hold for a second?

372
00:23:40,253 --> 00:23:41,921
Han Eun-young. Secretary Han.

373
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:47,218
THESE ARE PHOTOS I TOOK
OF THE RETAINED EARNINGS LEDGER

374
00:23:52,557 --> 00:23:54,725
We found another phone
belonging to Han Eun-young,

375
00:23:54,809 --> 00:23:57,478
and the last call was to you.

376
00:23:57,562 --> 00:23:59,438
We'd like you to come in for questioning.

377
00:23:59,522 --> 00:24:00,356
Okay.

378
00:24:07,155 --> 00:24:09,365
I told one other person besides you.

379
00:24:11,242 --> 00:24:12,451
Mr. Yoon's…

380
00:24:12,535 --> 00:24:15,538
Yoon Yi-jun's family?

381
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,124
Confidant?

382
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:21,586
Kim Si-hyun?

383
00:24:25,298 --> 00:24:27,925
He seemed to know everything,
yet somehow didn't know much.

384
00:24:32,597 --> 00:24:34,557
Whose side is he on?

385
00:24:46,527 --> 00:24:49,906
I got dumped
by a woman for the first time.

386
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:51,532
Do you also have a close friend?

387
00:24:54,619 --> 00:24:56,287
She also stabbed me in the back.

388
00:24:58,539 --> 00:24:59,582
It hurts.

389
00:25:01,042 --> 00:25:03,127
A friend who casually holds your hand.

390
00:25:03,211 --> 00:25:05,213
I don't chase women who leave.

391
00:25:05,296 --> 00:25:07,089
I've already come up with a conclusion

392
00:25:08,507 --> 00:25:11,344
on this useless confusion.

393
00:25:11,427 --> 00:25:13,471
He's cute like a little brother.

394
00:25:13,554 --> 00:25:17,892
I can even put up
with his stupid antics because of that.

395
00:25:17,975 --> 00:25:19,852
So why does this bother me?

396
00:25:20,937 --> 00:25:25,149
Why does he let just anyone
grab his hand like that?

397
00:25:25,816 --> 00:25:27,568
But why can't I move on?

398
00:25:27,652 --> 00:25:29,528
When we were leaving the restaurant…

399
00:25:29,612 --> 00:25:31,072
Yes, when we were leaving.

400
00:25:31,155 --> 00:25:32,907
We were leaving the police station…

401
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:35,743
Yes, we were leaving the police station…

402
00:25:36,577 --> 00:25:37,495
Police station?

403
00:25:38,287 --> 00:25:40,915
What police station? Tell me.

404
00:25:40,998 --> 00:25:43,542
-I…
-What police station?

405
00:25:44,252 --> 00:25:45,253
You were here?

406
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:47,713
How many times has this happened?

407
00:25:47,797 --> 00:25:51,926
When are you going to fix
this damn habit of causing trouble?

408
00:25:52,176 --> 00:25:54,095
Bong-yi, everyone at the company knows

409
00:25:54,178 --> 00:25:57,515
Yoon Yi-jun does whatever he wants.

410
00:25:57,598 --> 00:26:00,685
I'd say Jae-hee handled him pretty well.

411
00:26:00,768 --> 00:26:02,728
-You stand here as well.
-Sorry, Jae-hee.

412
00:26:06,274 --> 00:26:09,443
You went through all that trouble
to go undercover and find the phone.

413
00:26:09,527 --> 00:26:10,486
Why did you do this?

414
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:12,613
You're a cop
doing an undercover investigation.

415
00:26:12,697 --> 00:26:15,992
He's involved in the case,
and you brought him to your neighborhood,

416
00:26:16,075 --> 00:26:17,201
and the police station?

417
00:26:18,661 --> 00:26:19,620
I'm sorry, sir.

418
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:24,125
If you cause trouble one more time,
you're out of this case.

419
00:26:46,897 --> 00:26:48,316
You haven't gone home yet?

420
00:26:53,821 --> 00:26:54,697
Thank you.

421
00:26:56,157 --> 00:26:57,366
Let's go after Kim Si-hyun.

422
00:26:59,285 --> 00:27:01,287
I heard you're summoning Lee Hye-jung.

423
00:27:01,370 --> 00:27:03,873
-We're not waiting until then?
-We do both.

424
00:27:05,666 --> 00:27:07,293
We can't keep waiting.

425
00:27:08,044 --> 00:27:09,211
Right.

426
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:14,133
Earlier, I saw you two

427
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,011
in front of the office.

428
00:27:28,981 --> 00:27:31,359
-That's because Yoon Yi-jun--
-I trust you.

429
00:27:32,526 --> 00:27:33,944
But don't let him control you.

430
00:27:36,989 --> 00:27:38,908
Yes, sir. I'm sorry.

431
00:27:41,452 --> 00:27:42,745
Let's wrap this up quickly.

432
00:27:59,345 --> 00:28:02,139
Secretary Kang's close friend came running
to the police station,

433
00:28:02,223 --> 00:28:04,350
and you're actually jealous?

434
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:07,436
Jealous? I'm not crazy.

435
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:09,063
But why are you bothered?

436
00:28:10,398 --> 00:28:14,819
You said, "Why does he let just anyone
grab his hand like that?"

437
00:28:16,070 --> 00:28:17,488
How many times did I tell you?

438
00:28:17,571 --> 00:28:19,407
I like him as a little brother.

439
00:28:20,199 --> 00:28:21,659
He's cute like that.

440
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:23,786
Then don't be bothered by him.

441
00:28:24,370 --> 00:28:26,914
Who cares if he grabs or high-fives
another person's hand?

442
00:28:26,997 --> 00:28:28,416
He's just a little brother.

443
00:28:31,127 --> 00:28:34,338
Honey, does it bother you
if I hold another guy's hand?

444
00:28:34,422 --> 00:28:35,673
What if I was closer to him?

445
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:36,882
Who cares?

446
00:28:36,966 --> 00:28:39,260
See? You are jealous.

447
00:28:40,469 --> 00:28:43,097
You know what our brains do?

448
00:28:43,180 --> 00:28:45,599
They run on glucose

449
00:28:45,683 --> 00:28:48,310
just to trick their owners.

450
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:52,148
Tell yourself it's just affinity
or that he's cute like a little brother.

451
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:55,234
Deny it all you want.

452
00:28:56,694 --> 00:28:57,945
It only makes you miserable.

453
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:03,826
It'll just make you miserable.

454
00:29:17,047 --> 00:29:19,049
-Kim Si-hyun.
-Why is Attorney Kim

455
00:29:19,717 --> 00:29:21,302
in charge of the milk?

456
00:29:21,385 --> 00:29:23,095
Anyway, it's imported organic milk.

457
00:29:23,179 --> 00:29:25,931
And there's an imported food shop
around his place.

458
00:29:42,114 --> 00:29:44,408
Yesterday, you at least pretended
it was by accident.

459
00:29:44,492 --> 00:29:45,784
Now it's just blatant.

460
00:29:46,744 --> 00:29:48,537
You're telling me to stop playing dumb.

461
00:29:49,747 --> 00:29:52,333
Fine. Let's dig
into everything you've been hiding,

462
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:53,792
starting with Jerry's bowl.

463
00:29:54,293 --> 00:29:55,669
Why did you hide it?

464
00:29:55,753 --> 00:29:56,921
That night,

465
00:29:57,004 --> 00:29:59,840
I thought you were just being sensitive.

466
00:30:02,384 --> 00:30:04,970
It felt wasteful,
so I poured it for a cat.

467
00:30:05,054 --> 00:30:06,722
The bowl changed color the next day.

468
00:30:11,018 --> 00:30:14,813
So that's why you kept stopping me
whenever I picked up the milk,

469
00:30:15,356 --> 00:30:17,441
keeping an eye on me,

470
00:30:17,525 --> 00:30:20,444
and even asking
Manager Choi about Kim Si-hyun?

471
00:30:20,528 --> 00:30:21,737
That's right.

472
00:30:24,031 --> 00:30:25,241
Ding-dong.

473
00:30:27,576 --> 00:30:28,869
Milk delivery.

474
00:30:35,459 --> 00:30:36,877
That's enough.

475
00:30:43,926 --> 00:30:47,930
The only person who touches the milk
in this house is Mr. Yoon.

476
00:30:48,681 --> 00:30:51,559
Someone tampered with it
outside this house,

477
00:30:52,476 --> 00:30:53,519
from the very start.

478
00:31:07,825 --> 00:31:10,619
What if they targeted the end,
not the start?

479
00:31:12,204 --> 00:31:15,916
Why did you do things differently that day
instead of throwing out the milk

480
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:17,793
like you were told?

481
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,422
Are you suspecting me?

482
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:25,843
Secretaries obey Managing Director Yoon,
no matter how absurd it is.

483
00:31:25,926 --> 00:31:27,428
The legal team usually steps in

484
00:31:28,429 --> 00:31:31,307
when a VIP is involved,
like yesterday's police station incident.

485
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:33,642
But you talked him out of it.

486
00:31:35,102 --> 00:31:38,689
Mr. Kang, you always ignore protocol
and act independently.

487
00:31:40,566 --> 00:31:41,942
Is it just me who finds it odd?

488
00:31:42,693 --> 00:31:45,571
I admit I used poor personal judgment
at the police station.

489
00:31:45,654 --> 00:31:46,655
It won't happen again.

490
00:31:47,531 --> 00:31:48,824
But that bowl…

491
00:31:50,326 --> 00:31:52,411
That dish doesn't discolor that easily

492
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:54,622
just from having something on it.

493
00:31:54,705 --> 00:31:57,041
It was an attempt to harm Mr. Yoon.

494
00:31:57,124 --> 00:31:59,293
There's a weird rumor
among the secretaries

495
00:32:00,544 --> 00:32:02,838
about Attorney Kim and Ms. Yoon Na-jung.

496
00:32:05,549 --> 00:32:07,051
Enough, both of you.

497
00:32:08,135 --> 00:32:09,219
He is not…

498
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:11,555
the one.

499
00:32:12,306 --> 00:32:15,100
Why are you certain that he's not the one?

500
00:32:17,353 --> 00:32:18,771
Because I told him to.

501
00:32:20,731 --> 00:32:24,068
I told him to approach Na-jung.

502
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:27,905
I was getting excited
from being suspected.

503
00:32:28,906 --> 00:32:30,491
Is it fine to reveal it like this?

504
00:32:30,574 --> 00:32:33,452
-Get that milk off your chin.
-Okay.

505
00:32:33,535 --> 00:32:37,206
He kept an eye on you quietly because
he thought you were my confidant.

506
00:32:37,998 --> 00:32:39,625
He's not suspicious,

507
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:41,251
though he may be weird.

508
00:32:42,336 --> 00:32:43,629
You kept an eye on me?

509
00:32:43,712 --> 00:32:45,798
How exciting.

510
00:32:46,465 --> 00:32:48,217
Did you secretly watch me like this?

511
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:50,260
My heart is racing.

512
00:32:53,972 --> 00:32:54,932
What?

513
00:32:55,849 --> 00:32:57,476
-Hello, sir.
-Hello, sir.

514
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:00,187
I'll carry it for you, Ms. Lee.

515
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:04,983
Hello, Mr. Kang.

516
00:33:06,110 --> 00:33:08,404
Just asking out of genuine curiosity,

517
00:33:08,487 --> 00:33:09,988
but are you seeing anyone?

518
00:33:12,491 --> 00:33:13,367
What?

519
00:33:14,576 --> 00:33:15,452
Well…

520
00:33:17,955 --> 00:33:19,331
Breathe, Mr. Yoon.

521
00:33:22,334 --> 00:33:24,878
Mr. Yoon, this is today's schedule…

522
00:33:35,222 --> 00:33:37,433
You like him. That's love.

523
00:33:39,852 --> 00:33:41,228
You're not denying it anymore.

524
00:33:42,312 --> 00:33:43,397
Do you find this fun?

525
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,398
The fact that I…

526
00:33:45,149 --> 00:33:48,277
Seeing me like this over a guy
must be hilarious to you.

527
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:52,156
With AI replacing love in this new era
of the Fourth Industrial Revolution,

528
00:33:52,239 --> 00:33:54,408
what's the big deal
if it's between humans?

529
00:33:56,452 --> 00:33:58,454
Hey, Secretary Kang seems to be popular.

530
00:33:58,537 --> 00:34:00,080
You should've seen your face.

531
00:34:00,164 --> 00:34:03,000
You were so jealous.
I could feel the fire in your eyes.

532
00:34:04,835 --> 00:34:05,753
What about you?

533
00:34:06,336 --> 00:34:09,506
So it was Secretary Lee
who turned you down?

534
00:34:09,590 --> 00:34:11,842
It was way too obvious.

535
00:34:12,968 --> 00:34:15,387
"I got dumped. My heart aches."

536
00:34:16,305 --> 00:34:17,181
I know.

537
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:19,683
She gave the box to Secretary Kang
without hesitation.

538
00:34:20,517 --> 00:34:22,561
Nothing was ever that easy for me.

539
00:34:22,644 --> 00:34:24,688
Why are women like that?

540
00:34:24,772 --> 00:34:28,692
Why does everyone like Mr. Kang?
Never mind. You like him too, right?

541
00:34:30,861 --> 00:34:31,862
Get out!

542
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:33,530
Aren't you going to work?

543
00:34:34,531 --> 00:34:36,074
I will.

544
00:34:36,158 --> 00:34:38,160
We need to finish up our chat, though.

545
00:34:39,036 --> 00:34:40,579
I brought the milk every time.

546
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:42,831
No matter how much I think,

547
00:34:43,624 --> 00:34:45,542
I don't know how they tampered with it.

548
00:34:45,626 --> 00:34:47,044
How about we involve the police?

549
00:34:47,127 --> 00:34:49,546
No, if word gets out,

550
00:34:49,630 --> 00:34:51,924
the stocks will plummet,
including the subsidiaries.

551
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:53,926
But still…

552
00:34:57,846 --> 00:34:58,972
Hold on.

553
00:35:01,642 --> 00:35:02,726
Yes?

554
00:35:07,189 --> 00:35:10,192
I understand. I'll call you back.

555
00:35:14,863 --> 00:35:15,781
What is it?

556
00:35:18,033 --> 00:35:18,992
It's the police.

557
00:35:19,076 --> 00:35:20,911
They found Secretary Han's phone,

558
00:35:21,787 --> 00:35:23,622
so they're going to question the witness.

559
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,416
Who's the witness?

560
00:35:32,923 --> 00:35:35,175
-Mr. Kang.
-Yes?

561
00:35:36,468 --> 00:35:38,762
-Thank you for helping me.
-No problem.

562
00:35:39,596 --> 00:35:42,808
Can you check
Mr. Yoon's weekend schedule for me?

563
00:35:44,393 --> 00:35:47,896
The chairman wants to have a meal
with him and Director Lee Si-a.

564
00:35:50,649 --> 00:35:51,733
I see. I will do that.

565
00:35:53,318 --> 00:35:54,736
Right, Secretary Lee.

566
00:35:54,820 --> 00:35:57,739
Were you close to his secretary before me?

567
00:35:58,490 --> 00:35:59,741
Secretary Han?

568
00:36:03,412 --> 00:36:04,621
She was my first junior.

569
00:36:05,747 --> 00:36:06,957
But why do you ask?

570
00:36:07,499 --> 00:36:10,502
According to Secretary Jung,
you two were close.

571
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,963
You handled her things after she died.

572
00:36:13,714 --> 00:36:14,840
It must be hard for you.

573
00:36:43,785 --> 00:36:44,870
Lee Hye-jung.

574
00:36:51,084 --> 00:36:53,921
She's going in as a witness.
Nothing is set in stone.

575
00:36:57,883 --> 00:37:00,010
I shouldn't have wasted time
on other things.

576
00:37:01,845 --> 00:37:05,724
It didn't make sense from the start.

577
00:37:07,976 --> 00:37:10,520
I shouldn't have been confused
to begin with.

578
00:37:11,855 --> 00:37:13,273
Keep bringing the milk.

579
00:37:13,357 --> 00:37:15,651
It'd look weird
if you stopped bringing it.

580
00:37:15,734 --> 00:37:17,653
-As for Secretary Lee--
-I'll look into it.

581
00:37:35,087 --> 00:37:38,298
Mr. Yoon, I have a message
from the chairman's office.

582
00:37:38,382 --> 00:37:41,885
When would be a good time this weekend
to have a meal with Director Lee?

583
00:37:41,969 --> 00:37:43,345
Dinner on the 17th.

584
00:37:43,428 --> 00:37:45,222
I'll go with Secretary Jung. Don't come.

585
00:37:46,223 --> 00:37:47,891
It's okay. I can go with you, sir.

586
00:37:50,185 --> 00:37:51,645
I mentioned the discolored dish

587
00:37:51,728 --> 00:37:53,689
so that I can heighten security.

588
00:37:54,314 --> 00:37:56,441
We still don't know who did this.
It's dangerous.

589
00:37:56,525 --> 00:37:59,152
I understand that it is your job
to protect me.

590
00:37:59,236 --> 00:38:00,362
However,

591
00:38:00,445 --> 00:38:04,324
I don't remember giving you the right
to ignore my orders.

592
00:38:07,911 --> 00:38:08,870
Don't follow me out.

593
00:38:14,334 --> 00:38:15,627
What's with him again?

594
00:38:17,254 --> 00:38:19,214
Mom, is Uncle Yi-jun getting married?

595
00:38:20,048 --> 00:38:21,258
Si-a is in Korea.

596
00:38:22,384 --> 00:38:23,552
Si-a is?

597
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:27,472
Her comeback, the wedding announcement,
the shareholder meeting, and the election…

598
00:38:28,557 --> 00:38:29,683
It's perfect.

599
00:38:30,475 --> 00:38:33,103
But I kind of feel bad for Uncle Yi-jun.

600
00:38:33,186 --> 00:38:36,732
He doesn't get a say in his career
or even his marriage.

601
00:38:38,775 --> 00:38:41,194
I wonder if
Uncle has ever been in love for real.

602
00:38:51,580 --> 00:38:54,458
Think of it as a meeting between families.
Be there on time.

603
00:38:58,503 --> 00:39:00,756
I thought we had plenty of time
before the marriage.

604
00:39:01,798 --> 00:39:04,509
He'll win the election.

605
00:39:04,593 --> 00:39:06,845
Announce the wedding
before the shareholder meeting.

606
00:39:08,513 --> 00:39:10,098
And resume

607
00:39:13,268 --> 00:39:14,186
the share transfer.

608
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:15,896
Yes, sir.

609
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:23,236
Are you going to accept it?
Are you going to get married?

610
00:39:23,320 --> 00:39:26,406
He says he'll transfer the shares, so yes.

611
00:39:27,574 --> 00:39:30,410
That way, the desperate side
will start rushing.

612
00:39:31,745 --> 00:39:33,038
What about Na-jung?

613
00:39:33,121 --> 00:39:37,209
She knew Manager Park was digging
into the retained earnings ledger.

614
00:39:37,292 --> 00:39:39,002
Knowing about it is one thing.

615
00:39:39,086 --> 00:39:41,296
Stealing it herself is another.

616
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:43,924
How did she seem?

617
00:39:46,551 --> 00:39:49,096
She told me to bring Manager Park
and she'd tell me then.

618
00:40:06,488 --> 00:40:08,490
What if you had
taken over the company first

619
00:40:09,825 --> 00:40:12,077
and then started digging?

620
00:40:13,370 --> 00:40:15,080
Would it have been less dangerous?

621
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:18,083
No. I would've failed in both of them.

622
00:40:20,293 --> 00:40:22,796
In taking over the company
and finding the slush fund.

623
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:26,049
The money they hid
is just a means to an end.

624
00:40:26,133 --> 00:40:27,717
What is their end goal?

625
00:40:27,801 --> 00:40:29,219
To keep me from taking over.

626
00:40:30,637 --> 00:40:32,097
How scary.

627
00:40:33,723 --> 00:40:35,016
Taekang is so scary.

628
00:40:35,809 --> 00:40:37,769
TAEKANG CULTURAL FOUNDATION
SUPPORTS EX-CONS

629
00:40:42,357 --> 00:40:44,109
YOON NA-JUNG IS DRUNK ON POWER

630
00:40:47,904 --> 00:40:50,824
"Yoon Na-jung is drunk on power."

631
00:40:50,907 --> 00:40:52,659
I SAW HER SMOKING IN THE NO-SMOKING ZONE

632
00:40:52,742 --> 00:40:54,327
SHE WAS LUCKY ENOUGH TO BE BORN RICH

633
00:40:54,411 --> 00:40:56,830
Why are they throwing
a damn hissy fit here?

634
00:41:01,877 --> 00:41:04,254
THE USUAL PLACE AT SIX

635
00:41:20,228 --> 00:41:23,565
He managed to keep it a secret
all this time.

636
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:26,651
That's clever of him. So?

637
00:41:26,735 --> 00:41:30,572
Attorney Kim was flustered
and drank the milk.

638
00:41:31,198 --> 00:41:34,451
And as for Mr. Yoon…

639
00:41:34,534 --> 00:41:35,744
Well…

640
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:41,416
-Manager Choi.
-Yes?

641
00:41:43,752 --> 00:41:44,920
I make the judgment.

642
00:41:45,003 --> 00:41:46,880
Right, yes.

643
00:41:46,963 --> 00:41:49,758
Include all the details in your report.

644
00:41:49,841 --> 00:41:52,969
Nothing is free. You've received
the money from me until now.

645
00:41:54,930 --> 00:41:57,432
Mr. Yoon trusts Secretary Kang.

646
00:41:57,515 --> 00:42:00,143
He even vouched for him
in front of Attorney Kim.

647
00:42:02,479 --> 00:42:04,064
-He actually trusts someone?
-Yes.

648
00:42:07,025 --> 00:42:08,068
That secretary.

649
00:42:08,610 --> 00:42:11,571
-You mean Secretary Kang?
-From now on, put him on your watch list.

650
00:42:12,239 --> 00:42:13,490
Yes, ma'am.

651
00:42:23,750 --> 00:42:26,711
He was always acting suspiciously,

652
00:42:26,795 --> 00:42:29,297
so I thought
he was on Yoon Na-jung's side.

653
00:42:29,381 --> 00:42:31,258
If it wasn't Kim Si-hyun,

654
00:42:31,967 --> 00:42:34,094
then who put the herbicide in the milk?

655
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:39,474
Jae-hee.

656
00:42:41,935 --> 00:42:44,396
Remember what the captain
always used to say?

657
00:42:44,479 --> 00:42:45,897
Start from the beginning.

658
00:42:46,982 --> 00:42:48,692
By the way…

659
00:42:55,699 --> 00:42:57,033
you look wilted,

660
00:42:57,951 --> 00:42:59,744
like a weed pulled out by the roots.

661
00:42:59,828 --> 00:43:01,496
Is he giving you a hard time again?

662
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:03,707
He doesn't do that out of the blue.

663
00:43:04,666 --> 00:43:06,334
He's not that unreasonable.

664
00:43:07,669 --> 00:43:09,045
What did you say?

665
00:43:09,129 --> 00:43:10,630
Why are you standing up for him?

666
00:43:32,944 --> 00:43:34,237
Don't come in. Go home.

667
00:43:34,946 --> 00:43:36,406
I'll check the security system.

668
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:38,366
I said, do only what you are told.

669
00:43:40,994 --> 00:43:41,995
I'll admit.

670
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:44,247
I've been lenient recently.

671
00:43:44,331 --> 00:43:46,875
But I wasn't being lenient only with you.

672
00:43:46,958 --> 00:43:49,753
I was being less bitchy
to everyone else as well.

673
00:43:50,795 --> 00:43:53,965
Do you know what I found out
every time I did that?

674
00:43:56,426 --> 00:43:58,219
They all cross the line.

675
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:00,930
They don't know their place.

676
00:44:06,936 --> 00:44:09,356
You're hot one minute, cold the next.

677
00:44:09,439 --> 00:44:12,067
You're bearable one minute
and bitchy the next.

678
00:44:12,734 --> 00:44:14,235
He's driving me crazy.

679
00:44:15,362 --> 00:44:19,074
He's the one who kissed me,
talking about being brothers.

680
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:28,124
Hello?

681
00:44:51,356 --> 00:44:54,234
Didn't you say
you had something to say about Mr. Yoon?

682
00:44:54,317 --> 00:44:55,318
You know,

683
00:44:56,194 --> 00:44:58,863
I lie as easily as I breathe.

684
00:45:00,115 --> 00:45:01,699
I was afraid you wouldn't come.

685
00:45:01,783 --> 00:45:05,370
How can you dress so demurely
and lie through your teeth?

686
00:45:06,329 --> 00:45:09,416
It doesn't suit me, does it? I knew it.

687
00:45:10,375 --> 00:45:11,251
Wait here.

688
00:45:12,085 --> 00:45:13,753
What am I doing?

689
00:45:24,431 --> 00:45:27,851
To stand up to Chairman Yoon,
I have to dress like this.

690
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:30,061
It's for the family meeting.

691
00:45:30,145 --> 00:45:31,938
It's for the family meeting?

692
00:45:32,981 --> 00:45:34,691
They say it's just a meal,

693
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:37,026
but the bosses are meeting
to set the wedding date.

694
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:41,865
Why?

695
00:45:42,824 --> 00:45:43,950
Do you not like this one?

696
00:45:45,994 --> 00:45:48,371
No, that one is the prettiest. Ma'am?

697
00:46:33,708 --> 00:46:34,626
Secretary Kang.

698
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:37,170
Kang Jae-hee.

699
00:46:44,677 --> 00:46:45,678
You look pretty.

700
00:46:47,889 --> 00:46:50,099
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

701
00:46:50,183 --> 00:46:51,434
MOBILE PHONE FORENSIC REPORT

702
00:46:51,518 --> 00:46:53,186
DEVICE: SMARTPHONE
OWNER: HAN EUN-YOUNG

703
00:46:53,269 --> 00:46:54,729
CALL HISTORY

704
00:47:01,736 --> 00:47:04,155
We restored the deleted data
from Han Eun-young's phone.

705
00:47:04,239 --> 00:47:07,408
If your statement conflicts
with the files, it will work against you.

706
00:47:12,789 --> 00:47:13,957
Let's begin.

707
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:15,667
Are you Lee Hye-jung?

708
00:47:20,171 --> 00:47:21,381
Chief.

709
00:47:23,633 --> 00:47:24,509
Come in, please.

710
00:47:35,186 --> 00:47:38,022
Yes, she's in the investigation room.

711
00:47:39,190 --> 00:47:42,443
But an attorney
from the Taekang legal team

712
00:47:42,527 --> 00:47:44,028
just arrived.

713
00:47:46,239 --> 00:47:47,282
It's Kim Si-hyun.

714
00:47:49,242 --> 00:47:51,035
Open wide.

715
00:47:52,245 --> 00:47:55,206
I'd like to buy you meat
as the best shopping mate,

716
00:47:55,290 --> 00:47:56,958
but maybe next time.

717
00:47:57,041 --> 00:48:00,211
There was
only one reasonable choice anyway.

718
00:48:01,588 --> 00:48:04,424
As you know, it'll be
a very uncomfortable dinner for me.

719
00:48:04,507 --> 00:48:08,303
And I clearly stated
I won't eat or drink anything with you.

720
00:48:08,386 --> 00:48:10,638
The pastry here is good.
Eat up, my friend.

721
00:48:11,764 --> 00:48:13,391
And I never said I'd be your friend.

722
00:48:14,267 --> 00:48:17,770
If you don't have anything to discuss
regarding Mr. Yoon, I'm leaving.

723
00:48:19,188 --> 00:48:21,441
I know a little bit about Yoon Yi-jun.

724
00:48:22,650 --> 00:48:24,652
I knew him for quite some time.

725
00:48:34,412 --> 00:48:37,415
We're members of a social circle
for people from similar families.

726
00:48:37,832 --> 00:48:39,334
We went to school together too.

727
00:48:53,014 --> 00:48:54,182
Congratulations.

728
00:48:57,685 --> 00:48:58,686
Let's take a picture.

729
00:48:59,771 --> 00:49:01,648
One, two, three.

730
00:49:01,731 --> 00:49:03,983
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

731
00:49:04,067 --> 00:49:06,027
He's been like this since he was young.

732
00:49:07,362 --> 00:49:11,199
Even with a chauffeur-driven sedan
dropping him at school,

733
00:49:13,159 --> 00:49:16,663
he envied kids whose moms
came to pick them up with umbrellas.

734
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:22,585
Even with a top chef packing
a lavish spread for every picnic,

735
00:49:23,294 --> 00:49:25,046
he envied other kids' homemade gimbap.

736
00:49:26,506 --> 00:49:27,507
It's hunger.

737
00:49:28,091 --> 00:49:32,136
That hunger you only have
for things you've never had.

738
00:49:34,514 --> 00:49:36,432
He has enough money to buy everything,

739
00:49:36,516 --> 00:49:38,685
but he desires things
he can't buy with money.

740
00:49:39,352 --> 00:49:40,937
His instincts know

741
00:49:41,020 --> 00:49:43,398
what he can never buy with money.

742
00:49:46,234 --> 00:49:48,069
Why are you telling me this?

743
00:49:48,986 --> 00:49:50,988
Mr. Yoon may not want me to know.

744
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:53,324
I want to give him something he can't buy.

745
00:49:54,617 --> 00:49:57,537
I care about him a lot, you know.

746
00:50:03,876 --> 00:50:04,794
As for me,

747
00:50:05,670 --> 00:50:08,256
I'm getting married
so that I can be happier.

748
00:50:09,841 --> 00:50:11,801
Shouldn't it be the same for him?

749
00:50:18,850 --> 00:50:19,767
You're here.

750
00:50:20,518 --> 00:50:23,354
Didn't you tell me
who you were with so that I'd come?

751
00:50:31,237 --> 00:50:32,864
Why would you meet her?

752
00:50:32,947 --> 00:50:35,116
Why do you always do whatever you want?

753
00:50:35,658 --> 00:50:38,494
You're the one who told me
to give her my number.

754
00:50:38,578 --> 00:50:40,913
Does that mean
you can meet her separately?

755
00:50:40,997 --> 00:50:43,040
Do you think I wanted to meet her?

756
00:50:43,124 --> 00:50:46,461
How could I refuse
when she wanted to talk about you?

757
00:50:46,544 --> 00:50:48,254
Did you even want to refuse?

758
00:50:49,839 --> 00:50:51,674
You seemed like you enjoyed your time.

759
00:50:51,758 --> 00:50:53,176
Don't nitpick.

760
00:50:53,259 --> 00:50:55,052
Act like a secretary.

761
00:50:55,636 --> 00:50:57,805
Going on a date with Lee Si-a

762
00:50:57,889 --> 00:51:00,016
isn't part of your job.

763
00:51:00,099 --> 00:51:02,560
Then give me a chance to do my job.

764
00:51:02,643 --> 00:51:04,103
It's clear that you're in danger,

765
00:51:04,187 --> 00:51:05,813
but you're not letting me in!

766
00:51:05,897 --> 00:51:07,523
Just do what you're told!

767
00:51:07,607 --> 00:51:11,152
If I tell you not to come, don't.
If I tell you to go, go!

768
00:51:12,028 --> 00:51:14,781
If I can't talk to someone
who knows you well,

769
00:51:15,698 --> 00:51:17,074
what am I supposed to do?

770
00:51:19,952 --> 00:51:20,870
Forget it.

771
00:51:21,996 --> 00:51:23,998
If you're going to do whatever you want,

772
00:51:24,707 --> 00:51:26,793
just quit!

773
00:51:27,710 --> 00:51:29,962
Fine, I will.

774
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:32,840
I'm quitting.

775
00:51:34,342 --> 00:51:35,927
You little…

776
00:51:39,931 --> 00:51:41,516
I was mistaken for a moment.

777
00:51:47,271 --> 00:51:49,190
I thought maybe you were a good person.

778
00:52:04,747 --> 00:52:07,416
You'll get busy soon
with the election coming up.

779
00:52:09,377 --> 00:52:12,129
But nothing is more important
than your child's marriage.

780
00:52:12,964 --> 00:52:14,924
It's been a long time
since they got engaged.

781
00:52:15,007 --> 00:52:18,010
We should marry them soon.
How do you two feel about it?

782
00:52:23,015 --> 00:52:24,725
I'll do what Si-a wants.

783
00:52:27,979 --> 00:52:31,607
Chairman Yoon,
I'd like to receive one marriage gift.

784
00:52:32,191 --> 00:52:33,734
Do you want the entire company?

785
00:52:35,069 --> 00:52:38,322
I wouldn't refuse the offer,
but there's something else.

786
00:52:40,575 --> 00:52:41,534
I want Kang Jae-hee.

787
00:52:42,577 --> 00:52:45,371
He's Yi-jun's new secretary.

788
00:52:45,913 --> 00:52:47,164
He's very capable.

789
00:52:48,833 --> 00:52:50,001
Give him to me.

790
00:52:58,009 --> 00:53:00,094
Shakespeare once said,

791
00:53:00,887 --> 00:53:04,974
"If you can't remember the foolish things
you did for love,

792
00:53:05,057 --> 00:53:07,768
you've never been in love."

793
00:53:07,852 --> 00:53:10,813
What does that mean?

794
00:53:10,897 --> 00:53:11,939
Right?

795
00:53:12,023 --> 00:53:15,860
Whether you're the president, super rich,
or unemployed,

796
00:53:15,943 --> 00:53:18,362
we're all equally foolish

797
00:53:19,113 --> 00:53:21,449
when we're in love.

798
00:53:21,532 --> 00:53:23,284
EXPERT ON ROMANCE

799
00:53:23,367 --> 00:53:25,286
Stop saying foolish things.

800
00:53:25,369 --> 00:53:27,330
Don't bother me when I'm live streaming.

801
00:53:27,413 --> 00:53:28,664
What did you say?

802
00:53:29,999 --> 00:53:32,084
Before I fold you in half,

803
00:53:32,168 --> 00:53:34,253
go and see Jae-hee right now.

804
00:53:34,962 --> 00:53:37,423
Tomorrow is that day.

805
00:53:37,506 --> 00:53:38,925
Has it been a year already?

806
00:54:00,363 --> 00:54:01,656
Hello.

807
00:54:04,200 --> 00:54:05,242
It's Dad!

808
00:54:05,326 --> 00:54:07,787
-Dad!
-Hey, son!

809
00:54:07,870 --> 00:54:09,497
-Dad!
-There you are!

810
00:54:09,997 --> 00:54:11,499
-How are you?
-Good!

811
00:54:11,582 --> 00:54:13,459
-Should we go now?
-Yes.

812
00:54:14,126 --> 00:54:15,920
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

813
00:54:16,420 --> 00:54:17,421
Three points!

814
00:54:18,631 --> 00:54:20,007
Stop.

815
00:54:20,091 --> 00:54:22,760
-You're the best, Dad!
-That's it!

816
00:54:24,053 --> 00:54:24,929
Thank you.

817
00:54:26,347 --> 00:54:29,517
Dad, you said you were the best shot
in the military, right?

818
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:32,478
Of course. I landed every shot.

819
00:54:32,979 --> 00:54:33,980
Hi there.

820
00:54:36,357 --> 00:54:37,900
Son, come here.

821
00:54:38,734 --> 00:54:39,568
What's wrong?

822
00:54:40,111 --> 00:54:41,237
-Dad.
-Yes?

823
00:54:45,366 --> 00:54:47,410
Why is he so serious over a game?

824
00:54:50,997 --> 00:54:52,081
Should I show them?

825
00:54:52,164 --> 00:54:53,582
-Yes.
-Let's go.

826
00:54:55,084 --> 00:54:56,627
Up you go.

827
00:54:57,586 --> 00:54:58,629
Chin up!

828
00:55:00,172 --> 00:55:01,007
Five points!

829
00:55:02,425 --> 00:55:03,634
Five points!

830
00:55:04,427 --> 00:55:06,470
Another five! All five points!

831
00:55:08,264 --> 00:55:09,223
Dad!

832
00:55:12,309 --> 00:55:13,644
-Did you see?
-Yes.

833
00:55:13,728 --> 00:55:16,772
Son, I shot real guns in the army.

834
00:55:16,856 --> 00:55:18,524
It's way harder to shoot

835
00:55:18,607 --> 00:55:20,109
than toy guns like these.

836
00:55:20,192 --> 00:55:22,236
Then were you
in the special forces as well?

837
00:55:22,319 --> 00:55:23,487
What?

838
00:55:23,571 --> 00:55:26,073
Were you in the Special Mission Unit too?

839
00:55:26,157 --> 00:55:26,991
What?

840
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:29,326
-Dad.
-What?

841
00:55:29,410 --> 00:55:30,411
What's special forces?

842
00:55:30,494 --> 00:55:33,372
It's not better than
the army you were with, right?

843
00:55:33,456 --> 00:55:36,459
How about we go and have some churros?

844
00:55:36,542 --> 00:55:37,960
You came in first place today.

845
00:55:38,502 --> 00:55:40,421
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

846
00:55:41,297 --> 00:55:43,758
Son, there is a radio and goggles in here.

847
00:55:46,218 --> 00:55:47,428
How did I do?

848
00:55:47,511 --> 00:55:48,679
You're the best.

849
00:55:48,763 --> 00:55:49,889
High five!

850
00:55:49,972 --> 00:55:51,223
-Yes!
-Yes!

851
00:56:25,382 --> 00:56:26,383
Manager Choi.

852
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:30,179
I had no idea you were like this.

853
00:56:31,138 --> 00:56:32,264
Ma'am?

854
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:37,603
Hot coffee in this weather?

855
00:56:38,187 --> 00:56:39,105
Right.

856
00:56:40,106 --> 00:56:42,024
I'll bring iced coffee.

857
00:56:53,536 --> 00:56:55,246
Where's Secretary Kang?

858
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:58,999
I thought he would be working until today,
but I don't see him.

859
00:57:00,417 --> 00:57:01,669
What are you doing?

860
00:57:04,755 --> 00:57:07,424
I'm here to recruit Secretary Kang.

861
00:57:07,508 --> 00:57:10,594
I said I'd cooperate,
so why are you doing this?

862
00:57:13,430 --> 00:57:14,557
-Over there.
-There.

863
00:57:14,640 --> 00:57:16,475
-Look.
-There's a lion.

864
00:57:16,559 --> 00:57:18,144
It's a dad lion!

865
00:57:20,354 --> 00:57:22,523
-Its head is huge.
-It's a bear.

866
00:57:22,606 --> 00:57:24,608
A bear.

867
00:57:24,692 --> 00:57:26,861
-Its head is this big.
-It's this big.

868
00:57:26,944 --> 00:57:28,154
Look over there.

869
00:57:30,948 --> 00:57:32,575
The bear is standing up!

870
00:57:32,658 --> 00:57:33,826
Try roaring like a lion.

871
00:57:43,752 --> 00:57:46,338
Gosh, you look brave, son.

872
00:57:46,422 --> 00:57:47,965
Let's ride it again, Dad.

873
00:57:48,591 --> 00:57:49,800
-Again?
-Yes.

874
00:57:49,884 --> 00:57:51,010
Shall we?

875
00:57:51,969 --> 00:57:52,928
Okay, let's go.

876
00:57:53,762 --> 00:57:56,265
Hold on.

877
00:57:56,348 --> 00:57:57,933
DO NOT PICK UP

878
00:58:00,102 --> 00:58:01,020
Yes?

879
00:58:02,563 --> 00:58:04,023
I can't talk for long.

880
00:58:04,106 --> 00:58:06,609
Mr. Kang, are you at an amusement park?

881
00:58:08,777 --> 00:58:09,987
Fantasy Land?

882
00:58:13,657 --> 00:58:15,868
You're on a date?

883
00:58:18,287 --> 00:58:20,831
I guess you can't talk for long.
I'll get to the point.

884
00:58:20,915 --> 00:58:23,542
I'm offering double the salary
and triple the bonus.

885
00:58:24,501 --> 00:58:25,419
You accept?

886
00:58:26,462 --> 00:58:27,421
Good!

887
00:58:27,504 --> 00:58:30,090
Come to the art center
starting next week for work, then.

888
00:58:30,799 --> 00:58:32,218
Are you out of your mind?

889
00:58:33,219 --> 00:58:34,094
Hello?

890
00:58:34,887 --> 00:58:36,096
He hung up.

891
00:58:46,315 --> 00:58:47,566
He's not picking up?

892
00:58:48,317 --> 00:58:50,653
Well, there's no need for him
to pick up your call.

893
00:58:50,736 --> 00:58:52,071
He's mine now.

894
00:58:52,154 --> 00:58:54,406
He's not an object to stake a claim on.

895
00:58:57,076 --> 00:58:58,369
Pick up.

896
00:59:02,665 --> 00:59:05,376
-Did he really accept it?
-Yes.

897
00:59:07,336 --> 00:59:08,671
Just be honest.

898
00:59:11,257 --> 00:59:13,050
You don't want me to take him, do you?

899
00:59:13,133 --> 00:59:14,677
Don't treat him like a toy.

900
00:59:15,219 --> 00:59:16,637
Don't play with him.

901
00:59:17,137 --> 00:59:18,472
You like him,

902
00:59:20,015 --> 00:59:21,016
Kang Jae-hee.

903
00:59:31,402 --> 00:59:32,653
That's love.

904
00:59:33,445 --> 00:59:35,864
You like him,

905
00:59:36,407 --> 00:59:37,366
Kang Jae-hee.

906
00:59:58,387 --> 00:59:59,888
You can't see well, Jin-hyung?

907
00:59:59,972 --> 01:00:00,973
Hold on.

908
01:00:09,148 --> 01:00:10,983
It's fun, isn't it?

909
01:00:11,066 --> 01:00:12,860
-Not really.
-What?

910
01:00:12,943 --> 01:00:15,821
They are paid to do this.

911
01:00:15,904 --> 01:00:18,282
Wouldn't they be sad
if I acted like I was bored?

912
01:00:25,205 --> 01:00:26,123
Jin-hyung.

913
01:00:26,206 --> 01:00:29,251
-Let's go and find a better view.
-Yes.

914
01:00:29,960 --> 01:00:31,420
-Son, over there.
-Thank you.

915
01:00:32,046 --> 01:00:33,088
Look.

916
01:00:33,589 --> 01:00:35,049
Here you go.

917
01:00:35,132 --> 01:00:36,633
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

918
01:00:49,855 --> 01:00:50,898
Busted.

919
01:00:51,523 --> 01:00:53,025
Why did you pretend it's not fun?

920
01:00:53,817 --> 01:00:56,695
It's not that boring.

921
01:00:56,779 --> 01:00:58,322
Is it because you feel bad for Mom?

922
01:00:58,405 --> 01:00:59,323
Well…

923
01:01:01,450 --> 01:01:06,038
But your mom would rather see you
have fun.

924
01:01:06,705 --> 01:01:10,167
So don't lie and say
you're not having fun when you are.

925
01:01:11,251 --> 01:01:13,754
And don't hold back
when you want to do something.

926
01:01:14,546 --> 01:01:17,925
No, I didn't know
when I was six years old,

927
01:01:18,008 --> 01:01:20,094
but now I know that I am seven years old.

928
01:01:20,177 --> 01:01:24,014
If I say what's really on my mind,
Mom gets sad.

929
01:01:24,098 --> 01:01:27,643
When I tell her I miss Dad,
she becomes sad.

930
01:01:28,143 --> 01:01:31,271
But if you lie,

931
01:01:31,355 --> 01:01:33,148
the police officers will come get you.

932
01:01:33,232 --> 01:01:35,567
I'm going to arrest you, son.

933
01:01:36,568 --> 01:01:39,446
Have you never lied in your life, Dad?

934
01:01:39,530 --> 01:01:40,948
You've never lied to anyone?

935
01:01:48,414 --> 01:01:49,957
Look.

936
01:01:53,919 --> 01:01:55,504
My balloon!

937
01:01:56,004 --> 01:01:57,297
No!

938
01:01:57,381 --> 01:01:58,549
Son.

939
01:02:03,178 --> 01:02:04,138
Jin-hyung.

940
01:02:04,972 --> 01:02:06,723
-Thank you.
-Son.

941
01:02:08,684 --> 01:02:11,311
Dad, I'm here.

942
01:02:11,395 --> 01:02:14,148
I told you not to run
when there are a lot of people, son.

943
01:02:14,231 --> 01:02:15,357
Dad.

944
01:02:22,781 --> 01:02:23,699
"Son"?

945
01:02:26,869 --> 01:02:27,828
"Dad"?

946
01:03:09,286 --> 01:03:11,246
THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN, KIM DO-YOON,
JUNG YOO-MIN, PARK JUN-MUYN, YU SU-BIN

947
01:03:11,705 --> 01:03:13,707
Kang Jae-hee! Were you married?

948
01:03:13,790 --> 01:03:15,876
My boss has been a little bit weird.

949
01:03:15,959 --> 01:03:17,461
Don't make me worry.

950
01:03:17,544 --> 01:03:20,005
Here. Because you're cute.
I can buy you the whole thing.

951
01:03:20,088 --> 01:03:22,591
-That's the kind of boss I am.
-Do you like me?

952
01:03:23,133 --> 01:03:24,009
I'll meet them.

953
01:03:24,092 --> 01:03:25,344
It has a recording function.

954
01:03:25,427 --> 01:03:27,054
I'll be your lawyer, your ex,

955
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:29,097
whatever you need. So don't be scared.

956
01:03:29,181 --> 01:03:31,725
So maybe it's okay
to have Kang Jae-hee by my side.

957
01:03:31,808 --> 01:03:34,186
I guess I should expose that
you're a woman.

958
01:03:34,269 --> 01:03:36,522
-What's the problem?
-She should be your priority.

959
01:03:36,605 --> 01:03:38,524
So that I don't get the wrong idea.

960
01:03:38,607 --> 01:03:39,650
What?

961
01:03:39,733 --> 01:03:42,736
Translated by Leo Chung
